# AI Infrastructure Control - Environment Variables
#
# All AI provider keys and monitoring settings below are OPTIONAL.
# The app starts without them and falls back / disables features that need them.
# They are listed as comments (no "KEY=value") so deploy platforms don't
# auto-detect them as required. To use one, add it to your real .env or
# your host's environment settings.
#
# AI providers (set at least one to enable AI features):
#   GOOGLE_API_KEY      - Google Gemini, https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY    - DeepSeek
#   OPENAI_API_KEY      - OpenAI
#   XAI_API_KEY         - xAI (Grok)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   - Anthropic
#
# Grafana Cloud monitoring (Faro & OTel) - only initialised when set:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_FARO_URL         - Faro collector URL
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_FARO_APP_ID      - Faro app ID
#   OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT  - OTLP endpoint
#   OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS   - e.g. "Authorization=Basic <base64 auth>"

# Access control (see lib/api-guard.ts and proxy.ts):
#   APP_PASSWORD  - Password for the whole site (browser sign-in prompt, any username).
#                   REQUIRED in production for AI features: without APP_PASSWORD or
#                   API_SECRET, AI routes return 503 so nobody can spend your
#                   provider credits through a public URL.
#   API_SECRET    - Key for scripts/servers: "x-api-key: <key>" or "Authorization: Bearer <key>".
#   CRON_SECRET   - Vercel Cron sends "Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>" to /api/cron.
# Generate values with: openssl rand -base64 32

# Hermes Agent Configuration (Local)
HERMES_PATH=hermes
HERMES_PROJECT_DIR=.

# Environment
NODE_ENV=development
